    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `POST /api/owners` (and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back) return a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (with getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause `displayName` is derived in the mapper rather than persisted, it's populated on every owner serialization (create response and GET) and requires no changes to the `Owner` entity or the OfficeFloor function pipeline. The new `Cp05Tests` and all 11 existing tests pass.",
